{"reference":"Genesis 1","book":"Genesis","chapter":1,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"The image of God","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Genesis 1 presents humanity in the image of God. In later scriptural reception, the Messiah is called the image of the invisible God, and the new humanity is described as being renewed in knowledge according to the Creator's image. Those readings are disputed interpretations, so they should be kept distinct from the chapter's own wording.","verse_refs":["Genesis 1:26-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_001_976a8f95234b3b8868dc9e55"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
